{"type": "thinking", "text": "Interesting! Now history shows \"Today\" section expanded with Food $5, and 13 November section collapsed (because I collapsed it earlier!). Wait earlier after reopening from Analytics, the 13 November section was expanded (I observed \"Collapse 13 November\"). Then I closed, came back, entered an expense, and now when opening history, \"13 November\" is collapsed! So collapse state IS persisted across... hmm. Actually maybe the new entry today caused the sections' open set to change: opening today's section and maybe collapsing others? Hmm.\n\nWait sequence: Earlier, I collapsed 13 Nov, closed sheet, reopened sheet → 13 Nov expanded (observed \"Collapse\"). Then closed, went to main, added $5, went analytics, opened sheet → Today expanded, 13 Nov collapsed (element [9] \"Expand ... $60\"). Hmm, so state of section changed. Possibly when a new expense is added, only the new date section auto-expands and other sections collapse. That seems plausible design: on adding expense, open the today's section.\n\nHmm, but earlier I toggled the 13 Nov collapse state; then reopening showed expanded. So collapse state isn't persisted in memory across sheet close? But now 13 Nov collapsed. Confusing. Let me reason about the changed note: \"Expense history per-date sections: an empty open-sections set is now handled the same as a first visit.\" So first visit: open all sections? Wait on first visit (earlier) it showed 13 November expanded. When I collapsed it, open set became empty. On close & reopen, code checks if empty → treat as first visit? If first visit opens all, it should expand. And indeed after reopening it was expanded. So the \"empty set → first visit\" gives expand-all on open. Then why now collapsed? Because now open set is non-empty: {Today}? Hmm, when a new expense added today, maybe the state changed to open today's section only, leaving 13 Nov collapsed. But I collapsed 13 Nov manually and the set became empty; then when I closed, maybe app saved the empty set and then new expense set it to... hmm.\n\nActually wait, maybe the \"open sections\" set is per-sheet invocation, but when adding a new expense, the app sets open set to the new date section (Today). Then when I opened the sheet, Today expanded, 13 Nov collapsed. That's consistent.\n\nActually after my manual collapse and reopening, it showed expanded — consistent with \"empty → first visit expands all\". Then I closed. Did my manual collapse persist as empty? Perhaps after collapse, the internal set became empty, and then the sheet close saved it? Then opening after adding: hmm, the add probably added today's date to the open set before opening → non-empty → only Today open.\n\nAnyway, no obvious bug. Let's test the empty-set scenario more: collapse both sections so open set is empty; close; reopen → should expand all (same as first visit). Let's do that later.\n\nNow, more important: budget sheet inconsistency. Let's confirm after the $5: go to main, tap pill, see Spent. First close this sheet. Press back."}
