y=334) — fine. The \"Food\" chip at x=2223 extends to 2400 edge; the pill's right side is cut off (the rounded end may be beyond screen). That's minor.\n\nThe horizontal clipping of the \"Food\" chip could be a layout bug: chips row is wider than available (3 chips), so the last chip is clipped at the screen edge rather than wrapping/scrolling. With 4+ categories, more would be cut. But maybe row scrolls horizontally; the header category pill maybe partially offscreen by design (scrollable). Hmm.\n\nThe bigger concern: in the first landscape screenshot, the left pane showed \"Show subscriptions outside of...\" clipped by overlapping wavy lines. Now again \"v subscriptions outside of the period\" with wavy line covering the start. It seems the text is clipped horizontally at the pane boundary and the wavy decoration overlaps. That's a visual bug but perhaps not critical to the release areas.\n\nBut actually wait: In landscape, the left pane is showing the history — but the \"Show subscriptions outside of the period\" is a toggle at the bottom of history. The text is cut off: it starts with \"v subscriptions\" — the \"Sho\" is hidden behind a wavy line. That looks like an overlap/layout bug. Could report as cut_off/overlap in history screen in landscape. Hmm.\n\nBut before that: the main screen in landscape shows the *history panel* on the left even though I never opened it in this session state. That's the app's adaptive layout. Fine.\n\nLet me now focus on likely intended bugs. The changed items hint at where regressions are:\n1. Category management screen: categories loaded from DB on open. → maybe bug: new category doesn't show, or duplicates appear. Our test showed Entertainment appears in the grid AND in the quick chips (Transport/Entertainment/Food). Wait, quick chips show \"Transport, Entertainment, Food\" — order? Originally quick chips were Transport, Food. After adding Entertainment, order became Transport, Entertainment, Food. Hmm, alphabetical? Transport, Entertainment, Food is not alphabetical. Maybe order by created? Food, Transport originally; adding Entertainment at front? Hmm.\n\n2. Main screen number pad: new keypad component. → test 0, decimal, leading zeros, calc mode, backspace. So far all good. Maybe bug with the \"0\" key: when amount is \"\" and you tap 0, shows $0 (fine). Long press backspace clears (fine).\n\n3. Budget sheet summary rows include recurring templates → double count bug (found).\n\n4. History per-date sections empty open set → first visit behavior. Need to test: collapse all sections, close, reopen. Also with today + yesterday sections: collapse both, reopen should open all (first-visit behavior). Let's test and see if consistent. Also check for a bug where after collapsing all and reopening, sections show expanded but totals wrong? Hmm.\n\nLet me now test history thoroughly. Rotate back to portrait first. Also clear the $15 amount to avoid accidental submission. Long-press backspace [30] or [31]? In landscape elements: [30] Editor action @2132,701 is backspace (yellow X); [31] Editor action @2132,918 check. Long-press [30]."}
