 = $0.75\".\n\nThe first block uses $80 (which was budget sheet's Spent BEFORE today's $5). At that time, Analytics was $60. So the budget sheet's spent was $80 vs actual $60 — the $20 difference existed before.\n\nNow what's the $20? Could it be the recurring rent template scheduled for the NEXT period? Let me check the \"Show subscriptions outside of the period\" toggle. Maybe the history hides a subscription outside the period. Let me open history and enable \"Show subscriptions outside of the period\" to see if there's an extra $20 rent occurrence outside/inside. That toggle appeared only in landscape left pane. Hmm.\n\nActually, maybe the budget period started Nov 11 and the recurring Rent was an expense on Nov 13. But the recurring template might ALSO have a pending occurrence at Nov 13 (i.e., duplicate generated by the recurring engine) — one of them is the history entry $20; maybe there's a hidden \"subscription\" $20 shown when toggling \"Show subscriptions outside of the period\". If there are two rents, the budget should count both, and Analytics should too (but Analytics doesn't). Hmm.\n\nLet me look at the history with \"Show subscriptions outside of the period\". In portrait, the history sheet didn't show that toggle (only in landscape). Let me open history and rotate landscape to see, then toggle it.\n\nActually let me first delete today's test expense to restore base data, then reproduce cleanly from the precondition: budget sheet Spent vs history. Maybe the developer needs the clean state. Also the test category Entertainment remains — hmm, it's extra data but shouldn't affect totals.\n\nLet me delete the $6 expense. Navigate: total expenses → tap $6 → Delete. Currently main with $1 typed. Long-press backspace to clear. Then Analytics → scroll → Total Expenses → $6 item → Delete."}
