{"type": "thinking", "text": "Interesting! After reopening, the 13 November section is COLLAPSED (Expand), not expanded. This contradicts earlier behavior where reopening after collapsing all showed Today expanded. Wait earlier: after collapsing all (Today+13 Nov), closing, reopening showed Today expanded and 13 Nov collapsed. That is \"first visit\" maybe opens the latest date. Now with only 13 Nov, reopening shows it collapsed. So \"empty open set → first visit\" behavior appears broken now? Hmm.\n\nWait, but is the open set actually empty? The state persisted from previous session? We deleted today's expense; the open set may have been {Today}, and after deletion today's section is gone → open set may still contain \"Today\" (a date with no entries) — so not empty! Then on reopen, the set is non-empty ({Today}) but no matching section → all collapsed. That explains. So after deleting the last expense of a date, the open set still holds that date, causing a non-empty-but-stale set → all collapsed. Hmm, is that the \"empty open-sections set\" edge case? The change note might be about exactly this: an empty set should behave like first visit. But here the set is NOT empty; it contains a stale date. Hmm.\n\nBut the user-visible bug: after deleting the only expense and reopening history, the remaining date section is collapsed (shows just \"Expand 13 November $60\") instead of expanded (first visit). Is that a bug? It's arguably minor UX.\n\nHmm, but wait. Let me test the exact changed behavior from a clean state: collapse all, then close & reopen, and see. Earlier that worked (Today expanded). But now with only 13 Nov, let's collapse it and reopen. Does it expand? Let's test:\n\nCurrent: 13 Nov collapsed. Maybe the open set contains stale \"Today\". If I tap \"Expand 13 November\", it expands and adds 13 Nov to set. Then collapse it again → set may contain Today and 13 Nov? Hmm.\n\nLet me instead use the \"Close sheet\" X? Not present in this smaller sheet. Swipe down.\n\nSequence:\n1. Now: 13 Nov collapsed, open set likely {Today}.\n2. Tap Expand 13 Nov → open set {Today, 13 Nov}. Then tap Collapse → {Today}? So it may never empty. Hmm.\n\nThe empty set scenario requires removing Today from the set. How? Maybe open set is reset when all sections collapsed. Earlier, collapsing Today and 13 Nov gave empty → close/reopen → Today expanded. So empty works then. Now the set contains Today (stale) so it doesn't.\n\nPotentially reportable: after deleting the last expense of a date, the history sheet shows the remaining dates collapsed instead of honoring first-visit open state. But I'm not sure the expected behavior is \"expand\". The change note suggests: \"an empty open-sections set is now handled the same as a first visit.\" The stale-set case isn't empty. Hmm, not our changed item.\n\nLet me test the empty set behavior cleanly now: tap Expand 13 Nov (it opens), then tap Collapse (empty set). Close, reopen. If it expands → the fix works. Let me do that."}
